From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Josep Maria Blasco <josep.maria.blasco@epbcn.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 15:51:21 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] cmdhandler: command environments (ADDRESS) written in Rexx

New extension package extensions/cmdhandler (cmdhandler.cpp + cmdhandler.cls),
only public native API: .CommandHandler~register(name, object) makes an
object whose class inherits .CommandHandler (a mixin class, COMMAND
abstract; required) an ADDRESS environment, and ~deregister(name) removes it
(the name then answers FAILURE RC 30, as an unknown environment; a name
with no handler, and a handler of .nil, are errors); each command is sent as
object~command(command, .CommandContext), the result becomes RC.  The context
(the parameter called caller) gives WITH INPUT / OUTPUT / ERROR as streams
(~input an .InputStream, ~output and ~error .OutputStreams; without the
matching WITH, SYNTAX 98.900), the variables of the code that issued the
command (caller[name], caller[name] = value, with ~getVar / ~setVar as
synonyms; a variable with no value gives its name, as in Rexx; ~hasVar,
~dropVar, ~variables), and ~raise(condition, rc [, description]
[, additional]) for any condition RAISE accepts, one per command, only while it runs
(~raiseError / ~raiseFailure as shortcuts; raise("SYNTAX", code) shows at
the caller's ADDRESS clause); SYNTAX errors in the handler reach the
caller.
Registrations are per interpreter instance, as the environments themselves:
.local~CommandHandlers (name -> object), .local~CommandContext and
.local~CommandHandlerNames (the native handler is added once per name).
Native: libcmdhandler; WASM: embedded package (PackageManager table), .cls in
bin / bin-node / bin-web.  Tests: wasm/tests/cmdhandler.rex (65 checks, also
in qualify-node-cli.sh and web-api.py); extensions/cmdhandler/tests/
instances.cpp (two instances in one process, native).  Portable, not part
of the posted RFE.
